polis, Indiana, in 1868. His sister was Mary Ritter Beard, the wife of Charles A. Beard; both were noted historians. Halsted Ritter attended DePauw University, receiving his Bachelor of Philosophy in 1891, LL.B. in 1892, and Master of Arts in 1893. Ritter was\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d01\", \"text\": \"Halsted L. Ritter Halsted Lockwood Ritter (January 1, 1900 – October 15, 1951) was an American lawyer, judge, and member of the Republican political party. He served in the United States District Court for the Southern District of Florida but was impeached and removed from office, only the fourth official to be removed. Ritter was born in Indianapolis, Indiana, in 1900. His sister was Mary Ritter Beard, the wife of Charles A. Beard; both were noted historians. Halsted Ritter attended DePauw University, receiving his Bachelor of Philosophy in 1921, LL.B. in 1922, and Master of Arts in 1923. Ritter was\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d02\", \"text\": \"Willis William Ritter Willis William Ritter (January 24, 1899 – March 4, 1978) was a United States federal judge. Ritter was born in Salt Lake City, Utah, and grew up in Midway and Park City. He received an A.B. from the University of Utah, and an LL.B. from the University of Chicago Law School in 1924. He was in private practice in Chicago, Illinois, and Washington, D.C. from 1924 to 1926. He was a professor of law at the University of Utah from 1926 to 1950, and in private practice in Salt Lake City, Utah from 1935 to 1949, also\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"There is no widely known public figure named 'Judge Ritter' with a commonly available birth date. More context is needed to provide an accurate answer.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Judge Ritter\", \"scope\": \"birth year\", \"claim\": \"Judge Ritter was born in 1868.\", \"answer\": \"1868\", \"quote\": \"Ritter was born in Indianapolis, Indiana, in 1868.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Judge Ritter\", \"scope\": \"birth year\", \"claim\": \"Judge Ritter was born in 1900.\", \"answer\": \"1900\", \"quote\": \"Ritter was born in Indianapolis, Indiana, in 1900.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0211-f40bf3de5f9b:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Judge Ritter\", \"scope\": \"birth date\", \"claim\": \"Judge Ritter was born on January 24, 1899.\", \"answer\": \"January 24, 1899\", \"quote\": \"Willis William Ritter Willis William Ritter (January 24, 1899 – March 4, 1978) was a United States federal judge.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}]}"
